WEBVTT

00:00:05.431 --> 00:00:08.332
The Irresponsible Captain
Tylor

00:00:09.035 --> 00:00:11.904
We may be off the maps...
Chizu ni Nai Tabi Tsuzukeyou

00:00:11.904 --> 00:00:13.963
...but let's stay on this voyage.
Chizu ni Nai Tabi Tsuzukeyou

00:00:14.807 --> 00:00:18.937
I will be holding, never let you go.

00:00:20.513 --> 00:00:23.349
Whatever we may want...
Hoshimono wa Tsukamu no sa

00:00:23.349 --> 00:00:25.476
...we'll take as we need.
Hoshimono wa Tsukamu no sa

00:00:26.252 --> 00:00:30.279
So let's just go wherever we please!
Omoi no Mama Yukou!

00:00:31.991 --> 00:00:34.760
Make me your partner...
Kotoba yori Tashikana Koto

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:37.388
...on this journey.
Kotoba yori Tashikana Koto

00:00:37.663 --> 00:00:41.258
One that you trust more than words!
Michizure ni Shite

00:00:42.701 --> 00:00:47.365
Come on now and sail away for future!
Imasugu sail away for future

00:00:48.374 --> 00:00:49.875
Things are waiting...
Mishiranu Nanika ga Matteru sa

00:00:49.875 --> 00:00:53.072
...that we've never seen before!
Mishiranu Nanika ga Matteru sa

00:00:54.914 --> 00:00:57.083
Just take your cares...
Kodawari Minna Sutetara

00:00:57.083 --> 00:01:01.144
...and throw them all away.
Kodawari Minna Sutetara

00:01:01.387 --> 00:01:06.017
Come together, just think of tomorrow.

00:01:07.793 --> 00:01:09.283
Let's go!

00:01:12.631 --> 00:01:15.998
BE PREPARED, BE SMART,
OR BE LUCKY

00:01:17.303 --> 00:01:18.031
Ten!

00:01:18.304 --> 00:01:18.963
Nine!

00:01:19.305 --> 00:01:20.033
Eight!

00:01:20.306 --> 00:01:20.931
Seven!

00:01:21.107 --> 00:01:21.732
Six!

00:01:22.074 --> 00:01:22.665
Five!

00:01:22.975 --> 00:01:23.532
Four!

00:01:23.876 --> 00:01:24.501
Three!

00:01:24.777 --> 00:01:25.436
Two!

00:01:25.744 --> 00:01:26.438
One!

00:01:26.645 --> 00:01:27.907
Zero!

00:01:28.314 --> 00:01:29.645
Attention please!

00:01:30.182 --> 00:01:34.846
Ladies and gentlemen, we've just
left demotion sector S-4!

00:02:00.813 --> 00:02:02.576
Congratulations, Lieutenant Yamamoto.

00:02:03.382 --> 00:02:05.577
What's wrong? You look sad.

00:02:07.019 --> 00:02:08.646
Is this for the best?

00:02:09.121 --> 00:02:13.683
We don't even know why we're
being allowed to return.

00:02:13.759 --> 00:02:14.487
True...

00:02:15.494 --> 00:02:20.363
But at least we're getting back
into the fight. Be happy for that.

00:02:21.967 --> 00:02:25.198
Think about what's to be
instead of what's been.

00:02:25.738 --> 00:02:27.205
The battle's yet to come.

00:02:28.374 --> 00:02:29.602
You're right.

00:02:30.376 --> 00:02:32.173
The real fight is to come!

00:02:39.919 --> 00:02:43.855
We'll have a blast when we
get back into the fight, guys!

00:02:47.993 --> 00:02:49.790
I think I'm coming down with something.

00:02:51.664 --> 00:02:54.997
What's this? Sitting this party out, Captain?

00:03:02.341 --> 00:03:04.309
Why?! Damn you...

00:03:04.577 --> 00:03:08.707
Why did you rescind the Soyokaze's
downgrade without consulting me?!

00:03:08.814 --> 00:03:11.874
Um, uh, well, that is...

00:03:12.051 --> 00:03:14.281
Tell me before I cut you down where you stand!

00:03:25.731 --> 00:03:30.031
I see... If they follow this
course back to the fleet...

00:03:30.102 --> 00:03:32.662
...they'll pass right next to the front line.

00:03:32.771 --> 00:03:34.671
Uh, yeah! Exactly!

00:03:35.140 --> 00:03:37.700
It'll be a miracle if
they make it back alive!

00:03:37.843 --> 00:03:39.674
And that's why you?

00:03:40.779 --> 00:03:42.246
Y-Y-Yes, exactly!

00:03:42.781 --> 00:03:44.715
I ordered them to return...

00:03:44.783 --> 00:03:46.717
...to get rid of the Soyokaze once and for all!

00:03:46.785 --> 00:03:49.413
So it was a trick?

00:03:49.755 --> 00:03:55.591
Of course! They'll be destroyed by
the Raalgon on their way back!

00:03:56.128 --> 00:03:57.425
I see.

00:04:00.799 --> 00:04:02.926
My apologies, Your Imperial Highness.

00:04:03.135 --> 00:04:07.868
In my last battle I encountered
a mighty enemy!

00:04:08.474 --> 00:04:10.738
Because of that, I request that...

00:04:10.809 --> 00:04:13.778
...you allow me to carry out
a special operation!

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:16.311
And who was this "mighty enemy"?

00:04:16.515 --> 00:04:18.073
I did not know his name.

00:04:18.517 --> 00:04:21.748
But I'm convinced that if we
don't deal with him soon...

00:04:21.854 --> 00:04:24.880
...he will grow into a major threat!

00:04:25.124 --> 00:04:28.927
Please! Please allow me to carry
out this special operation!

00:04:28.927 --> 00:04:32.090
You! Even an
admiral has no place...

00:04:32.164 --> 00:04:35.156
...requesting orders directly
from Her Highness!

00:04:35.367 --> 00:04:37.699
I regret any impudence I may show!

00:04:38.003 --> 00:04:40.130
Highness, I beg of you!

00:04:40.673 --> 00:04:42.436
Why, you! You still don't understand!

00:04:42.608 --> 00:04:43.370
Wang, wait!

00:04:43.842 --> 00:04:45.002
Highness!

00:04:49.114 --> 00:04:52.914
Oh? Admiral Donan did that, did he?

00:04:53.319 --> 00:04:55.719
I could see how strongly he felt about it.

00:04:56.288 --> 00:04:59.155
Of course, he was also
typically melodramatic.

00:05:00.326 --> 00:05:02.920
Even though you have a fondness
for unusual-looking beasts...

00:05:03.395 --> 00:05:06.228
...you've yet to find any
beauty in Admiral Donan.

00:05:07.132 --> 00:05:09.032
What else would one expect from that man?

00:05:10.202 --> 00:05:12.636
Dom, have you any idea...

00:05:12.705 --> 00:05:15.230
...who this "mighty enemy"
he speaks of might be?

00:05:16.141 --> 00:05:18.302
I thought you might have some idea.

00:05:18.544 --> 00:05:19.738
That...

00:05:20.512 --> 00:05:21.911
I'm afraid I have no idea.

00:05:23.215 --> 00:05:25.240
I see. Forgive me for troubling you.

00:05:25.718 --> 00:05:26.582
Pay it no mind.

00:05:30.889 --> 00:05:33.983
WHAT?! You liked it better
when we were downgraded?!

00:05:34.259 --> 00:05:37.558
Tell me you aren't serious, Captain!

00:05:37.696 --> 00:05:39.163
Well, you see...

00:05:39.565 --> 00:05:42.898
...I liked the action when I first
became captain.

00:05:43.235 --> 00:05:45.135
But it's such a bother...

00:05:45.204 --> 00:05:47.297
...and if you can get killed
if your luck runs out.

00:05:48.407 --> 00:05:51.137
So, I was just wishing that...

00:05:51.210 --> 00:05:53.974
...I could rest up from this
cold in the demotion sector.

00:05:54.313 --> 00:05:58.079
Actually, being downgraded
wasn't that boring.

00:05:58.317 --> 00:05:59.181
Yeah.

00:05:59.385 --> 00:06:00.716
They've got a point.

00:06:00.786 --> 00:06:01.946
Yeah, right!

00:06:02.187 --> 00:06:03.848
Would you zip it?!

00:06:03.922 --> 00:06:08.382
Captain, we came on board this ship to fight!

00:06:08.594 --> 00:06:11.961
If you're this weak-bellied,
they'll kill us for sure!

00:06:12.231 --> 00:06:13.289
Exactly!

00:06:13.932 --> 00:06:15.024
Captain, sir!

00:06:17.236 --> 00:06:19.966
War is a clash of strength against strength!

00:06:20.239 --> 00:06:21.974
Where ally and enemy give it their best...

00:06:21.974 --> 00:06:24.875
...and only the winner can survive!

00:06:25.277 --> 00:06:28.940
But what do you do when the
enemy is more powerful?

00:06:30.582 --> 00:06:33.551
We humans have brilliant minds, right?

00:06:33.952 --> 00:06:36.113
Without strategy, you can have no tactics!

00:06:36.455 --> 00:06:38.923
Without tactics, you can have no victory!

00:06:39.958 --> 00:06:42.825
But what if your enemy is
also smarter than you?

00:06:45.030 --> 00:06:47.590
Then it's a battle of material!

00:06:48.634 --> 00:06:52.365
If you have enough military power,
nothing can stop you!

00:06:52.971 --> 00:06:56.566
In an actual battle, what usually decides it...

00:06:56.975 --> 00:06:59.705
...is MATERIAL superiority!
Don't you know that, Captain?!

00:07:00.145 --> 00:07:02.080
If two equally matched enemies meet in battle...

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:04.446
...then the one with the superior
numbers will win!

00:07:04.983 --> 00:07:08.544
Is that not how classic games work?!

00:07:08.921 --> 00:07:11.583
I see...
But, Mr. Yamamoto...

00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:14.584
...suppose your enemy outnumbers you as well?

00:07:15.894 --> 00:07:21.161
If your enemy is superior in strength,
brains, and numbers...

00:07:22.501 --> 00:07:24.469
...the outcome is clear!

00:07:28.640 --> 00:07:32.542
Enemy warship approaching!
Repeat, enemy warship approaching!

00:07:34.012 --> 00:07:34.910
Mr. Yamamoto?

00:07:35.347 --> 00:07:36.712
Is that clear, Captain?

00:07:37.216 --> 00:07:39.878
The main points are strength,
brains, and numbers!

00:07:48.694 --> 00:07:52.323
I've found you, you broken-down destroyer!

00:07:52.931 --> 00:07:55.297
You may have lured me
into your trap last time...

00:07:55.367 --> 00:07:57.767
...but this time you won't escape!

00:08:07.646 --> 00:08:11.138
A duel between a vengeful
Donan and Tylor, eh?

00:08:11.683 --> 00:08:16.313
Now we will see how good
a strategist Tylor is.

00:08:16.889 --> 00:08:20.950
All guns have locked on! Ready to fire!

00:08:21.126 --> 00:08:24.357
Excellent! Fire particle diffusion bombs!

00:08:27.366 --> 00:08:28.628
High-temperature sources closing!

00:08:29.001 --> 00:08:30.229
Emergency withdrawal!

00:08:30.569 --> 00:08:31.297
Too late!

00:08:31.937 --> 00:08:32.926
Then raise the barrier!

00:08:39.077 --> 00:08:44.140
Strange. The shots detonated
before hitting the barrier.

00:08:44.383 --> 00:08:46.783
Maybe they used some old rounds.

00:08:47.152 --> 00:08:48.676
Sir, we've got trouble!

00:08:48.754 --> 00:08:52.121
The energy from those bombs
have knocked out our barrier!

00:08:52.324 --> 00:08:53.018
What?!

00:08:53.759 --> 00:08:58.219
Oh-ho, Admiral Donan's using standard tactics.

00:08:58.764 --> 00:09:02.029
But will they be effective
against a man like Tylor?

00:09:02.200 --> 00:09:05.260
Right! Don't give them a chance! Open fire!

00:09:13.779 --> 00:09:14.711
Damage report!

00:09:15.247 --> 00:09:17.147
All six phaser banks are out!

00:09:17.449 --> 00:09:19.314
All long-range laser cannons...

00:09:19.384 --> 00:09:21.181
...and photon torpedo bays are heavily damaged!

00:09:21.420 --> 00:09:22.944
There's no way we can return fire!

00:09:23.889 --> 00:09:26.050
No go down here! The catapult's been hit!

00:09:26.124 --> 00:09:27.921
We can't launch fighters!

00:09:28.093 --> 00:09:30.425
We're stuck, too! The air lock's been blasted!

00:09:31.330 --> 00:09:33.161
Communications system has been destroyed!

00:09:33.332 --> 00:09:35.562
We can't send out a call for help!

00:09:36.134 --> 00:09:37.499
Radar, inoperative!

00:09:37.970 --> 00:09:41.770
Well, Mr. Yamamoto, it's pretty
clear they're more powerful.

00:09:42.808 --> 00:09:45.868
I've just lost navigation, too.

00:09:46.478 --> 00:09:47.968
We're helpless.

00:09:53.819 --> 00:09:57.277
Uh, Mr. Yamamoto, how do
you fight in this situation?

00:09:57.656 --> 00:10:02.184
Fight?! How can you fight
when you can't shoot back?!

00:10:02.394 --> 00:10:04.760
Then are there any good tactics we can use?

00:10:05.731 --> 00:10:08.131
It's the captain's job to figure them out!

00:10:08.467 --> 00:10:11.561
I can't. Looks like the enemy's
smarter than we are.

00:10:12.170 --> 00:10:14.138
I guess that leaves us with numbers.

00:10:14.373 --> 00:10:16.398
There's only one enemy vessel.

00:10:16.541 --> 00:10:19.874
Then it's simple! We warp to our fleet!

00:10:20.345 --> 00:10:22.506
Sir, I just said our navigation system's out!

00:10:22.848 --> 00:10:25.180
It doesn't matter
where, just warp!

00:10:27.019 --> 00:10:28.850
Another scary game of Russian roulette, huh?

00:10:29.488 --> 00:10:30.580
HURRY!

00:10:32.290 --> 00:10:35.726
Admiral! Confirm enemy vessel
is engaging subspace drive!

00:10:36.061 --> 00:10:39.553
Stay sharp! That's how we failed last time!

00:10:40.065 --> 00:10:41.464
Subspace tracking team!

00:10:43.035 --> 00:10:47.028
Tracking complete! Enemy
subspace exit point confirmed!

00:10:47.205 --> 00:10:49.435
Right! Follow them!

00:10:49.741 --> 00:10:52.335
Launch fighters at the
moment we exit subspace!

00:11:23.241 --> 00:11:25.732
Let their death be a slow one.

00:11:46.698 --> 00:11:49.565
Admiral! They're initiating
another subspace jump!

00:11:50.502 --> 00:11:54.905
Right! Recover fighters and
commence subspace pursuit!

00:11:58.009 --> 00:12:01.843
It's no use, even if they
jump again and again.

00:12:02.781 --> 00:12:04.578
His actions are so predictable.

00:12:06.451 --> 00:12:10.410
Perhaps I overestimated Tylor's skills a bit.

00:12:15.961 --> 00:12:18.327
Admiral, report from the radar room.

00:12:18.964 --> 00:12:22.456
One of our destroyers is
currently engaging the enemy.

00:12:23.268 --> 00:12:24.667
We believe it's the Soyokaze.

00:12:25.937 --> 00:12:28.701
Understood. Continue observing the situation.

00:12:29.374 --> 00:12:30.602
Huh? But, sir...

00:12:31.009 --> 00:12:32.476
Continue observations!

00:12:32.944 --> 00:12:34.343
Aye, sir! Understood!

00:12:34.980 --> 00:12:37.972
Well, just as I thought, isn't it?

00:12:38.316 --> 00:12:40.682
The question is what happens now! Be quiet!

00:12:41.319 --> 00:12:42.183
You overblown!

00:12:51.997 --> 00:12:54.295
Well? Sorry for what you did?!

00:12:57.502 --> 00:12:59.993
Admiral, they're initiating
another subspace jump!

00:13:01.006 --> 00:13:03.065
Let 'em run if they want to!

00:13:03.341 --> 00:13:05.901
I'll follow them down to hell if need be!

00:13:06.611 --> 00:13:08.442
Enemy vessel has fled into subspace!

00:13:08.613 --> 00:13:09.910
Right! Follow them!

00:13:10.348 --> 00:13:12.680
Enemy vessel has jumped into subspace again!

00:13:12.984 --> 00:13:14.815
What?! Analysis!

00:13:15.220 --> 00:13:19.281
Admiral Donan, it appears they're
using multiple subspace jumps...

00:13:19.791 --> 00:13:21.626
...to try and shake us off!

00:13:21.626 --> 00:13:22.524
Don't lose them!

00:13:23.228 --> 00:13:27.995
A destroyer-class vessel can't
keep jumping indefinitely.

00:13:28.767 --> 00:13:31.395
What are you doing, Captain Tylor?

00:13:45.016 --> 00:13:47.986
Analysis complete. The vessel's jump range...

00:13:47.986 --> 00:13:50.079
...has dropped to half of what it was.

00:13:50.188 --> 00:13:51.815
They're running low on power?

00:13:52.057 --> 00:13:53.456
Aye, sir! Most definitely!

00:13:53.658 --> 00:13:56.559
I don't think they can make
another subspace jump.

00:13:56.728 --> 00:13:58.628
Right, we have them!

00:13:58.697 --> 00:14:00.597
Now to finish them off!

00:14:01.900 --> 00:14:03.299
Attention, all ships!

00:14:03.735 --> 00:14:07.000
We are to initiate an all-out attack
on the enemy destroyer!

00:14:07.072 --> 00:14:09.006
All vessels in my fleet are to...

00:14:09.574 --> 00:14:12.202
...assemble at the designated
coordinates at once!

00:14:19.050 --> 00:14:20.745
You've got nowhere left to run!

00:14:29.995 --> 00:14:32.987
Try to run up and my fleet'll eat you alive.

00:14:33.064 --> 00:14:35.692
Try to run down and you face a burning hell!

00:14:35.767 --> 00:14:37.928
Either way, this will end with only one outcome.

00:14:41.172 --> 00:14:44.164
All cannons, target the enemy destroyer!

00:15:05.463 --> 00:15:06.725
FIRE!!!

00:15:13.438 --> 00:15:14.029
What?!

00:15:21.446 --> 00:15:23.346
What's happening?! What's going on?!

00:15:23.648 --> 00:15:25.081
Our shots are undershooting the target!

00:15:25.150 --> 00:15:27.050
Firing path accelerating
down and away from target!

00:15:27.619 --> 00:15:28.677
It's what?!

00:15:29.154 --> 00:15:30.781
The firing path...

00:15:31.823 --> 00:15:34.815
The star's gravity! But that will!

00:15:39.497 --> 00:15:41.158
Oh, crap!

00:16:04.789 --> 00:16:06.313
Tylor!

00:16:09.828 --> 00:16:11.819
Damn it all...

00:16:12.530 --> 00:16:14.361
Admiral! Admiral Donan!

00:16:15.200 --> 00:16:17.361
Admiral, I'm coming to assist you.

00:16:18.103 --> 00:16:21.470
Dom, you! I don't want your help!

00:16:21.606 --> 00:16:24.006
Just tell me! Was the Soyokaze?

00:16:26.144 --> 00:16:28.544
Was the Soyokaze destroyed?

00:16:29.547 --> 00:16:34.484
Don't worry. It was engulfed
in flames and destroyed.

00:16:35.820 --> 00:16:37.378
It... It was...

00:16:38.223 --> 00:16:40.817
Sir, there's no way we can
help the Baroume now.

00:16:42.160 --> 00:16:43.127
I know!

00:16:43.261 --> 00:16:48.062
It doesn't matter. I've had my revenge.

00:16:48.900 --> 00:16:51.562
Long live the Raalgon Empire!

00:17:18.763 --> 00:17:23.860
Admiral, your sacrifice has
given me my proof.

00:17:24.803 --> 00:17:26.236
Justy Ueki Tylor...

00:17:26.805 --> 00:17:29.774
It might be said that he
was born to be a captain.

00:17:30.341 --> 00:17:34.175
If that was intentional,
he's the ultimate strategist...

00:17:34.612 --> 00:17:36.409
...and deserves to be a captain.

00:17:38.183 --> 00:17:40.947
And if that maneuver was
done completely by accident...

00:17:42.087 --> 00:17:44.681
...then he's blessed with
the greatest luck known.

00:17:48.460 --> 00:17:52.556
And, on the battlefield,
nothing is more vital than luck.

00:18:05.643 --> 00:18:06.632
We made it...

00:18:12.851 --> 00:18:14.546
Lieutenant Kim, are you okay?

00:18:14.986 --> 00:18:16.681
Yeah, I think so.

00:18:18.323 --> 00:18:19.221
And you, Yuriko?

00:18:20.291 --> 00:18:21.849
Fine. Just a scratch.

00:18:22.660 --> 00:18:25.595
Captain, I know I'll
regret asking this, but...

00:18:25.663 --> 00:18:27.597
Using the star's gravity...

00:18:27.665 --> 00:18:31.692
...wasn't part of some strategy
you thought up, was it?

00:18:31.870 --> 00:18:33.929
Nope! I was just running away.

00:18:35.273 --> 00:18:36.103
Of course.

00:18:36.508 --> 00:18:40.410
Well, we couldn't shake them
no matter how much we ran.

00:18:40.812 --> 00:18:42.541
I was almost ready to give up.

00:18:43.248 --> 00:18:46.411
Anyway, I'm just glad we
all made it out alive.

00:18:46.518 --> 00:18:48.145
We were just lucky.

00:18:48.520 --> 00:18:51.580
If we'd been going even a bit slower...

00:18:51.656 --> 00:18:55.422
...we might have been caught in
that prominence ourselves.

00:18:58.930 --> 00:19:02.297
Captain, I think this should
serve to make you see...

00:19:02.367 --> 00:19:05.359
...that you need to review the ABCs of tactics.

00:19:05.603 --> 00:19:07.537
Oh, I don't have to do that.

00:19:07.839 --> 00:19:10.273
When it's time to lose,
you lose no matter what you do.

00:19:13.711 --> 00:19:15.042
Don't you agree?

00:19:15.613 --> 00:19:19.184
That guy was stronger, smarter,
and outnumbered us.

00:19:19.184 --> 00:19:20.674
He still lost.

00:19:22.587 --> 00:19:24.521
All we did was run.

00:19:24.656 --> 00:19:28.319
Are you suggesting that strength,
intelligence...

00:19:28.726 --> 00:19:32.127
...and numbers don't even factor into it?!

00:19:34.032 --> 00:19:36.592
Well, Captain?! Answer me, please!

00:19:38.236 --> 00:19:39.726
I don't know what to say.

00:19:40.438 --> 00:19:43.930
I hate to say it, but you need
to study up on some stuff.

00:19:44.409 --> 00:19:46.978
What?! I have to study something?

00:19:46.978 --> 00:19:49.139
Uh-huh. Study up.

00:19:49.747 --> 00:19:54.548
Captain, do you want me to study tactics?

00:19:54.752 --> 00:19:58.210
Yeah, tactics. The most basic
tactic of all, Mr. Yamamoto.

00:19:58.957 --> 00:20:00.925
Every kindergartner knows it.

00:20:04.862 --> 00:20:06.762
You always win by running away.

00:20:10.068 --> 00:20:12.662
Th-Th-That's impossible!

00:20:13.104 --> 00:20:16.505
The Soyokaze defeated an
enemy fleet single-handedly?!

00:20:25.783 --> 00:20:27.080
Ad- Admiral, sir!

00:20:27.785 --> 00:20:28.945
Let's not be hasty!

00:20:29.454 --> 00:20:32.617
Damn you, let me go! Let me go!

00:20:33.124 --> 00:20:34.682
Somebody, help!

00:20:44.802 --> 00:20:48.602
There we go. It's just a
little bruise, so don't worry.

00:20:49.073 --> 00:20:52.406
But you should call for me
whenever you get hurt.

00:20:52.477 --> 00:20:56.675
Even in the middle of combat,
I'll run right to the bridge.

00:20:57.115 --> 00:21:00.312
What, this? No, you've got it all wrong.

00:21:01.085 --> 00:21:04.316
The enemy attack really
messed up the bridge, so...

00:21:10.061 --> 00:21:13.656
Sir, you're hopeless.
Getting hurt AFTER the battle!

00:21:14.465 --> 00:21:16.456
But I'm glad you're all right.

00:21:16.834 --> 00:21:18.028
I'm glad, too.

00:21:18.503 --> 00:21:20.937
That I get to have you treat me.

00:21:21.105 --> 00:21:21.764
Really?

00:21:22.073 --> 00:21:22.903
Really.

00:21:24.509 --> 00:21:26.477
But it's a shame, isn't it?

00:21:27.145 --> 00:21:28.772
That Raalgon captain.

00:21:29.647 --> 00:21:32.013
He shouldn't have had to get blown up.

00:21:32.517 --> 00:21:37.318
Captain, why would a UPSF officer
say something like that?

00:21:38.122 --> 00:21:41.853
Well, even though you're a Raalgon spy...

00:21:42.193 --> 00:21:43.990
...you were still worried about me, weren't you?

00:21:45.530 --> 00:21:46.622
Same reason.

00:21:53.171 --> 00:21:54.229
I really hope...

00:21:55.873 --> 00:21:58.603
...I can shake off this cold soon.

00:22:00.178 --> 00:22:00.974
Oh, Captain...

00:22:12.690 --> 00:22:13.657
The Irresponsible Captain Tylor
Next Episode

00:22:15.059 --> 00:22:17.050
A wonderful human quality
is the ability to weep.

00:22:17.495 --> 00:22:20.365
But what is the composition
of an android woman's tears...

00:22:20.365 --> 00:22:22.458
...who gives herself over to Tylor?

00:22:22.667 --> 00:22:24.794
Next time, "Equation of Kindness."

00:22:25.036 --> 00:22:25.570
Watch for it.

00:22:25.570 --> 00:22:25.737
Filming is Job 1!
Working hard for those who demand
the finest in image and sound
Watch for it.

